<title>NEW ZEALAND: Housing NZ, HCNZ and Community Housing to merge.</title>
<headline>Housing NZ, HCNZ and Community Housing to merge.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Housing Minister Murray McCully said on Monday that the government had moved to merge Housing New Zealand, Housing Corp of New Zealand and Community Housing Ltd.</p>
<p>Michael Cashin, chairman of HCNZ and CHL, will be chairman of Housing New Zealand, replacing Fran Wilde, recently appointed chief executive of Tradenz.</p>
<p>The move had been flagged in the government coalition agreement.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
